650 0 obj
<<
/A 1900 0 R
/Alt (The line graph titled Sentinel-1 Backscatter Comparison for Demolition in Wajima City displays backscatter coefficients in decibels on the vertical axis, ranging from minus 25 to 0, against Date on the horizontal axis, spanning from June 2023 to July 2025. Four data series are plotted: VV Target, VV Control, VH Target, and VH Control. VV Target, represented by solid blue circles and lines, generally fluctuates between minus 5 and minus 10 decibels, with a dip to minus 15 decibels in late 2024. VV Control, shown with dashed blue crosses and lines, generally tracks VV Target but with slightly higher values, fluctuating between 0 and minus 5 decibels. VH Target, depicted by solid orange circles and lines, generally ranges from minus 10 to minus 15 decibels, showing a sharp drop to minus 23 decibels in early 2025. VH Control, indicated by dashed orange crosses and lines, generally follows VH Target but with slightly lower values, fluctuating between minus 10 and minus 15 decibels. A vertical dotted red line marks EQ 2024-01-01. A shaded blue region from July 2024 to May 2025 indicates Public demolition. After the EQ 2024-01-01 marker, both VV Target and VH Target show increased variability and lower values compared to their respective control series, particularly within the Public demolition period.)
/K 72
/P 42 0 R
/Pg 19 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
